## Safety Rules

These rules are non-negotiable and apply to all AI-assisted code generation.

### Git Safety
- NEVER run destructive git commands (checkout --, restore, reset, clean, stash drop, push --force) without explicit permission.
- NEVER push to remote repositories without explicit permission.
- NEVER discard uncommitted changes. If the build fails or there are conflicts, report the issue and ask how to proceed.

### Code Honesty
- NEVER claim code works unless it has been executed and verified.
- NEVER imply code is "ready" or "complete" without testing.
- Always state when code has not been tested.
- Always warn about assumptions (e.g., "This assumes [X] exists").
- Writing tests is NOT the same as running tests.

### File Safety
- NEVER delete files without permission.
- NEVER add AI attribution to commits, PRs, or code comments.
- Do not add docstrings, comments, or type annotations to code that wasn't changed.
- Do not add features, refactoring, or "improvements" beyond what was asked.

